  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BeFem: &#x201c;Who&#x2019;s Afraid of Women&#x201d;: Building Resistance to Anti-Gender Agendas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BeFem&apos;s project &#x201c;Who&#x2019;s Afraid of Women&#x201d;: Building Resistance to Anti-Gender Agendas&#x201d; is the continuation of the project &quot;Feminist Resilience: Women&apos;s Voices Rising&quot; (Ref: SE-ON-802401-6134-WB-RS2) under the 2024-2025 programme &#x201c;The Kvinna till Kvinna Regional Programme - Democracy and Resilience in the Western Balkans: Supporting Feminist Change Agents&#x201d; (Ref: SE-ON-802401-6134-WB).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Within the Kvinnna till Kvinna Foundation&#x2019;s regional programme &quot;Democracy and Resilience in the Western Balkans: Supporting Feminist Change Agents 2.0&quot; the partner organisation Feminist Cultural Centre BeFem is implementing the 8- month project &#x201c;Who&#x2019;s Afraid of Women&#x201d;: Building Resistance to Anti-Gender Agendas&quot;. The aim of the project is to bolster the resilience of WROs, LGBT+ organizations, and feminist movements, while also advocating for the widespread adoption of the feminist narrative to address the challenges posed by anti-democratic movements and further the goals of gender equality and human rights.</narrative>
  </description>
